; ===========================================================================
; DLTX addon for Sych's trade file (zat_b30_owl_stalker_trader).
; Adds the artefact containers to his assortment.
;
; WHY THIS FILE HAS NO "!#include" AND NO SECTIONS OF ITS OWN
;   The engine opens its trade file by the path
;   configs\misc\trade\trade_zat_b30_stalker_trader.ltx, which is provided by
;   the addon ixray-stcop-wp-3.7-cop-r1.0. While reading that root file the
;   engine automatically looks for "mod_<rootfile>_*.ltx" in the same folder and
;   picks up THIS file (its name matches mod_trade_zat_b30_stalker_trader_*.ltx,
;   Xr_ini.cpp:1138). So the file is loaded by itself - no include needed.
;
;   DO NOT add "#include "trade_zat_b30_stalker_trader.ltx"" here: the engine
;   would read the base file a SECOND time and die with
;       FATAL ERROR, Xr_ini.cpp:1071
;       Duplicate section 'trader' wasn't marked as an override
;   (that is exactly what happened on the first attempt).
;
; HOW THE ADDITIONS WORK
;   A line starting with ">" does not declare a section: the engine appends the
;   value to the list of the section named after ">" and splits it by commas
;   (Xr_ini.cpp:445 and 371). So we only list our own entries and never repeat
;   the 1476-line trade table.
;   NOTE: the header is ">[section]", NOT "[>section]" - the latter would be read
;   as a section literally named ">section" (same family of mistakes as
;   "![Name]" vs "[!Name]", see MEMO 20).
;
; WHAT SYCH TRADES
;   Empty containers only. Combos (an artefact inside a container) have
;   can_trade = false, so they are neither offered nor bought.
;
; PRICES
;   The player BUYS an empty container for its full cost:
;     field 15000, universal 25000, scientific 40000.
;   The player SELLS it back at 60% (9000 / 15000 / 24000) - the same rate Sych
;   buys artefacts at, so reselling is never profitable.
; ===========================================================================

; What Sych pays the player (item cost * factor)
>[trade_generic_buy]
>bq_field_container = 1, 0.6
>bq_uni_container   = 1, 0.6
>bq_sci_container   = 1, 0.6

; What Sych is willing to sell (stock comes from the supplies list below)
>[trade_generic_sell]
>bq_field_container
>bq_uni_container
>bq_sci_container

; Stock: count, probability
>[supplies_generic]
>bq_field_container = 2, 1.0
>bq_uni_container   = 1, 0.2
>bq_sci_container   = 1, 0.05
